"Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Property claim valuation","Snow load damage","Earthquake claims","Remote construction costs"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}],"priceRange":"$$"},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Alaska Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/#webpage","url":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/","name":"Insurance Appraisal Process in Alaska | 8 Steps","description":"The insurance appraisal process in Alaska step by step: the written demand, naming appraisers and an umpire, negotiation and the binding award.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-12","primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/#primaryimage"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/#howto"}},{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/#primaryimage","url":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/clipboard-notes.webp","contentUrl":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/clipboard-notes.webp","width":1200,"height":800,"caption":"Worker in a high-visibility vest writing on a clipboard over construction plans"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Appraisal process","item":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/"}],"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How the insurance appraisal process works in Alaska","description":"The eight stages of a property insurance appraisal, from the disagreement to the signed award.","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Pin down the disagreement","text":"Appraisal resolves the amount of loss. Before anything else, confirm that coverage is accepted and that the dispute is about scope or price. Get the carrier's full itemized estimate in writing."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Build your own number","text":"Get an independent, line-item estimate that reflects current costs where the property is, including freight, travel and seasonal access when they apply."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Send a written demand","text":"Follow your policy's appraisal clause. Most require a written demand. Keep a copy and proof of delivery."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Name the appraisers","text":"Each side appoints its own appraiser, often within a set number of days of the demand. Your appraiser should meet the policy's independence requirement."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"Select an umpire","text":"The two appraisers try to agree on a neutral umpire. If they cannot, many policies let either side ask a court in the state where the property is located to appoint one."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"Appraisers work the differences","text":"The appraisers inspect, exchange estimates and go line by line. Most items are usually resolved at this stage."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":7,"name":"Umpire decides what is left","text":"Remaining items go to the umpire with supporting photos, measurements and pricing. The umpire may inspect the property."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":8,"name":"Signed award and payment","text":"An award signed by any two of the three sets the amount of loss. Payment then follows under the policy terms, subject to deductibles, limits and depreciation."}],"@id":"https://alaskainsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-clause-process/#howto"}]}</script>
